Let us note that if $\mathfrak{M}$ , $\mathfrak{M}^{\prime}$ are two symplectic resolutions of $\mathfrak{M}_{0}$ , then the algebras $H^{*}_{S_{\mathfrak{M}_{0}}}(\mathfrak{M},\mathbb{C})$ , $H^{*}_{S_{\mathfrak{M}_{0}}}(\mathfrak{M}^{\prime},\mathbb{C})$ are isomorphic. This follows from the fact that the universal deformations $\mathfrak{M}_{\mathfrak{t}_{\mathfrak{M}_{0}}}ightarrow\mathfrak{t}_{\mathfrak{M}_{0}}$ , $\mathfrak{M}^{\prime}_{\mathfrak{t}_{\mathfrak{M}_{0}}}ightarrow\mathfrak{t}_{\mathfrak{M}_{0}}$ are locally trivial in $C^{\infty}$ -topology (see [NAM2, Section 1.2 and references therein]), so $\mathfrak{M}$ , $\mathfrak{M}^{\prime}$ are both diffeomorphic to a generic fiber of $\mathfrak{M}_{0,\mathfrak{t}_{\mathfrak{M}_{0}}}ightarrow\mathfrak{t}_{\mathfrak{M}_{0}}$ . We are grateful to Pavel Etingof for explaining this to us.
Similarly, one can see that for any generic cocharacter $
u\colon\mathbb{C}^{	imes}ightarrow S_{\mathcal{M}}$ the schematic fixed points $\mathcal{M}_{\mathfrak{t}_{\mathcal{M}}}^{
u(\mathbb{C}^{	imes})}$ are the same and are isomorphic to the schematic fixed points $\mathcal{M}_{\mathfrak{t}_{\mathcal{M}}}^{S_{\mathcal{M}}}$ . Indeed, note that $\mathcal{M}_{\mathfrak{t}_{\mathcal{M}}}$ can be $S_{\mathcal{M}}$ -equivariantly embedded in some vector space $O$ with a linear action of $S_{\mathcal{M}}$ . Then $\mathcal{M}_{\mathfrak{t}_{\mathcal{M}}}^{
u(\mathbb{C}^{	imes})}$ , $\mathcal{M}_{\mathfrak{t}_{\mathcal{M}}}^{S_{\mathcal{M}}}$ are (schematic) intersections

$\mathcal{M}_{\mathfrak{t}_{\mathcal{M}}}^{
u(\mathbb{C}^{	imes})}=\mathcal{M}_{\mathfrak{t}_{\mathcal{M}}}\cap O^{
u(\mathbb{C}^{	imes})},~\mathcal{M}_{\mathfrak{t}_{\mathcal{M}}}^{S_{\mathcal{M}}}=\mathcal{M}_{\mathfrak{t}_{\mathcal{M}}}\cap O^{S_{\mathcal{M}}}.$

This reduces the claim to showing that $O^{
u(\mathbb{C}^{	imes})}=O^{S_{\mathcal{M}}}$ for a generic $
u\colon\mathbb{C}^{	imes}ightarrow S_{\mathcal{M}}$ that directly follows from Proposition 1.6 since $O$ is smooth. We are grateful to Alexander Braverman for explaining this to us.
